This pull request introduces support for a new staging environment in the deployment pipeline, updates deployment workflows to better handle multiple environments, and improves the reliability of Lambda function deployments. The most important changes are grouped below by theme.

Deployment Pipeline and Environment Support:

Added a staging environment to the deployment workflow options in .github/workflows/deploy.yml, and updated the workflow to ignore pushes to the main branch. [1] [2]
Defined staging configuration in config/environments.yml, including AWS region and API Gateway settings.
Added staging Lambda function names to config/lambdas.yml for both policy_graph_ingest and soap_verification functions.
Deployment Reliability Improvements:

Enhanced scripts/deploy_lambda.sh to wait for the Lambda version to become active before updating the alias, and added retry logic to the alias update step for improved robustness.
