This retry loop can roll the live alias back to an older version when two workflow runs deploy the same Lambda concurrently: an earlier run that fails here can retry after a later run has successfully moved live to a newer version, and this unconditional update then overwrites it. The workflow has no per-Lambda concurrency control; serialize deployments or re-check/guard the alias version before retrying.

